  <section id="purpose" class="doc-section">
    <h2>What the mesh kernel is</h2>
    <p>The mesh kernel works on closed triangle meshes: it builds them from parametric primitives (<code>meshOf</code>), measures them (<code>meshVolume</code>, <code>meshBounds</code>, <code>meshTopology</code>), and combines them with Booleans (<code>booleanMesh</code>, <code>booleanAll</code>). It is what the viewport shows, what the CAM generators machine, and what STL export writes.</p>
    <p>It is not an exact boundary representation. A cylinder that was cut stays a faceted cylinder, and there is no face topology to fillet or measure on. For exact faces, fillets, mass properties and STEP, the <a href="/docs/kernels/brep">B-rep kernel</a> is a separate piece of code.</p>
