  <section id="topology" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Topology check</h2>
    <code>meshTopology</code> counts vertices, edges and triangles, finds boundary, non-manifold and mis-oriented edges, degenerate triangles and shells, and derives Euler characteristic and genus. <code>describeTopology</code> prints the one-line summary the assistant and the viewport use.
    <DocCode language="json" title="meshTopology(bored) — real output">
{"{\u0022vertices\u0022:312,\u0022triangles\u0022:640,\u0022edges\u0022:960,\u0022boundaryEdges\u0022:0,\u0022nonManifoldEdges\u0022:0,\n \u0022misorientedEdges\u0022:0,\u0022degenerateTriangles\u0022:0,\u0022shells\u0022:1,\u0022eulerCharacteristic\u0022:-8,\u0022genus\u0022:5,\n \u0022closed\u0022:true,\u0022solid\u0022:true,\u0022volume\u0022:23981.43509870267,\u0022area\u0022:8238.640705862534}\n// describeTopology \u2192 \u0022closed solid, 1 shell, genus 5, 640 triangles, V 23981.4 mm\u00b3, A 8238.6 mm\u00b2\u0022"}
    </DocCode>
    <p>V − E + F = 312 − 960 + 640 = −8 = 2 − 2g, so g = 5: the four drilled holes plus the bore, which runs through the boss and the plate.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="triangulate" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Polygon triangulation</h2>
    <code>triangulatePolygon(outer, holes)</code> returns index triples into the concatenation of the outer ring and the holes. A 4 × 4 square with a 2 × 2 hole gives eight triangles:
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Real output">
{"triangulatePolygon(\n  [{x:0,y:0},{x:4,y:0},{x:4,y:4},{x:0,y:4}],\n  [[{x:1,y:1},{x:1,y:3},{x:3,y:3},{x:3,y:1}]])\n// [[0,4,5],[7,4,0],[3,0,5],[7,0,1],[2,3,5],[6,7,1],[2,5,6],[6,1,2]]"}
    </DocCode>
    <code>triangulatePolygonChecked</code> returns <code>undefined</code> instead of a partial result when the input cannot be triangulated (self-intersecting rings, holes outside the outer ring).
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Boolean result has holes or flipped faces</td><td>an input is open or wound clockwise</td><td>check both inputs with meshTopology: boundaryEdges and misorientedEdges must be 0</td></tr>
        <tr><td>a face shared by both operands is missing or doubled</td><td>the faces are nearly but not exactly coincident (farther apart than the tolerance)</td><td>snap the operands to the same plane, or raise CsgOptions.tolerance</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RangeError: Mesh tolerance exceeds subdivision budget</td><td>tolerance far too fine for the radius</td><td>use the tolerance presets (0.1 to 0.0005 mm)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>volume differs from the formula</td><td>faceting at coarse tolerance</td><td>mesh finer, or use the B-rep kernel for exact mass properties</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Boolean slow on many tools</td><td>union of tools built first</td><td>subtract tools one by one (booleanAll does this): each convex tool is a handful of planes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

